      "reasons": [
        "The definition adds an unsupported explanatory gloss (“lessons learned from earlier encounters”) that is not stated in the source.",
        "The source supports a historical claim about early experience making external action the method adopted when possible, but it does not directly support the broader formulation that this is a general lesson about how a person or animal later acts.",
        "The phrasing “teaching that action is the practical way to obtain pleasure or avoid pain” overstates the source; the passage says experience leads the organism to adopt external action to realize pleasure or suppress pain, not that early experience itself is a teaching process."
